From 5482f65374e92ec24fb80486bc8a54aca1d48713 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:54:03 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(2d): judge a Trochoidal slot against the finished part
 like the Slot

The Trochoidal slot's endpoints and width are typed by hand, but its
depth law fell to DepthLaw::None: a whole-model slot through a pocket
wall posted with the stock aligned or turned, and one 3 mm under the
floor posted with the stock turned (the program sim refuses to judge).
depth_law_of now routes it through authored_law (Entity/Selection ->
Section, Stock -> None) after the part_solid early return, so the op
carries blocking gouges and the post is refused by name. #1513's
slot_fit refusal for a picked region is unchanged.

Audit of the 2D kinds still at None is pinned in authored_law_tests;
Engrave/Trace on a whole model filed as #1595.

Fixes #1593

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL
